course: dictionary
lesson: 10804
title: Varied: many different kinds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Varied means made of many different kinds of things. A varied diet has lots of different foods in it, not just one or two. «Today most children who eat a varied diet get their vitamins from food» tells you that eating many different foods gives you what you need.
explain: Varied can also be the past form of vary, which means to change or to be different. Vary, varies, varied and varying all come from the same idea. «The temperature varied during the day» means it went up and down, so it was not the same all day.
explain: Look at the words around varied to find its meaning. If the sentence is about lots of different foods, varied means mixed. If it is about things changing, varied means changed. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Varied means made of many different kinds.
fact: Varied is also the past form of vary: it changed or was different.
fact: Vary means to change or be different. Varies means changes now. Varying means changing. Varied means changed before.
fact: «Good zoos breed to keep rare animals healthy and varied» means the zoo wants many different kinds of animals, and healthy ones.
fact: In science, you change (vary) one thing at a time. «The results varied» means the results were not all the same.
exercise: «Today most children who eat a varied diet get their vitamins from food.» What does varied mean in this sentence? | Shut away from others | *Made of many different kinds | Very loud | Very old
exercise: «The temperature varied during the day.» What does varied mean here? | Was shouted loudly | *Changed, or was different | Went very cold and stopped | Stayed exactly the same
exercise: In a science test, Sam changed one thing and says, «The results varied.» What does this mean? | Sam wrote them in pencil | *The results were not all the same | The results were all exactly the same | The results were lost
test: «Ben's mood varies a lot from day to day.» What does varies mean? | Sleeps | Stays still | Shouts | *Changes
test: What does varied mean in «a varied mix of fruit, bread and fish»? | Wrapped up | Dull and plain | Very hot | *Many different kinds
exam: Which word is the past form of vary? | Varying | Varies | Variety | *Varied
